└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST endpoints
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client() vs requests.Session() have different constructor defaults (e.g. connection pooling, base_url handling); Timeout semantics 
    │   differ: requests uses a single float or tuple, httpx uses httpx.Timeout objects with more granular control; Exception hierarchies differ: requests 
    │   raises requests.exceptions.HTTPError, httpx raises httpx.HTTPStatusError -- error handling code must be updated; httpx also supports async clients 
    │   (httpx.AsyncClient) but this file's usage is entirely synchronous, so only the sync Client API is a valid substitute
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses requests.Session() to perform blocking GET calls with a timeout, then calls raise_for_status() and json() on the response. httpx.Client()
        supports the same synchronous method signatures (get, raise_for_status, json), making it a plausible substitute for this specific usage pattern 
        (docstring itself calls this out as the intended substitution target).

